Description: PGO: do not use the training profile of ld/ldelf.c
 --enable-pgo-build=lto trains the freshly built ld by running the ld
 testsuite with -fprofile-generate and rebuilds it with -fprofile-use.
 ld/ldelf.c is the only translation unit of ld whose counters are not
 derived from test input shipped in the source package: whenever a
 DT_NEEDED entry cannot be resolved, ldelf_parse_ld_so_conf parses
 /etc/ld.so.conf and every file this includes, so its profile also depends
 on the build host.  That is where the two 20261029_215922 debrebuild runs
 differ: ldelf_parse_ld_so_conf grows from 728 to 729 bytes and its .cold
 part from 317 to 320, which moves 190 later symbols and changes .text,
 .rodata, .eh_frame, .rela.dyn, .data and .note.gnu.build-id.
 .
 Verified on a local build with the same flags: the same profile gives byte
 identical binaries, replacing only ld/ldelf.gcda gives a different one,
 and the ASLR dependent value profile payloads that do differ between two
 identical training runs do not change the output at all.
 .
 ld/ldelf.gcda is dropped between the training run and the -fprofile-use
 rebuild, so this translation unit is optimized from static heuristics like
 untrained code and its layout no longer follows a profile input that the
 source package does not fully determine.
Author: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
Last-Update: 2026-10-30
---
diff --git a/Makefile.in b/Makefile.in
index 38f1f9ab..65bbdd7c 100644
--- a/Makefile.in
+++ b/Makefile.in
@@ -1168,6 +1168,7 @@ all:
 		$(PGO_BUILD_TRAINING_MFLAGS) \
 		$(PGO_BUILD_TRAINING_FLAGS_TO_PASS) \
 		$(PGO_BUILD_TRAINING) \
+	&& rm -f ld/ldelf.gcda \
 	&& $(MAKE) $(RECURSE_FLAGS_TO_PASS) clean \
 	&& $(MAKE) $(RECURSE_FLAGS_TO_PASS) \
 		$(PGO_BUILD_USE_FLAGS_TO_PASS) all-host all-target \
diff --git a/Makefile.tpl b/Makefile.tpl
index 88db8f44..72a1ef20 100644
--- a/Makefile.tpl
+++ b/Makefile.tpl
@@ -851,6 +851,7 @@ all:
 		$(PGO_BUILD_TRAINING_MFLAGS) \
 		$(PGO_BUILD_TRAINING_FLAGS_TO_PASS) \
 		$(PGO_BUILD_TRAINING) \
+	&& rm -f ld/ldelf.gcda \
 	&& $(MAKE) $(RECURSE_FLAGS_TO_PASS) clean \
 	&& $(MAKE) $(RECURSE_FLAGS_TO_PASS) \
 		$(PGO_BUILD_USE_FLAGS_TO_PASS) all-host all-target \
